   "id": 615414,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In  the 1840s and 1850s, the existence of the Missouri Compromise line at 36°30′ led to ",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1169628,
     "content_html": "strong Northeastern support for the Mexican-American War"
    },
    {
     "id": 1169629,
     "content_html": "reluctance of southerners in Congress to organize territories north of the line"
    },
    {
     "id": 1169627,
     "content_html": "relaxation of slave laws in the cotton-rich South"
    },
    {
     "id": 1169626,
     "content_html": "expansion of cotton cultivation north of the Mason-Dixon line"
    }
   ],
